# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything NOT excluded here ends up in an
# image layer and stays extractable with `docker history` / `docker save` even if
# a later layer deletes it. Treat this file as a security control, not as a
# build-speed optimisation.
#
# Order matters: a later pattern overrides an earlier one. The negations that the
# Visual Studio scaffold put at the bottom of this file (re-including .git/config,
# which routinely holds a remote URL with an embedded PAT) have been removed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local configuration — MUST come first and MUST NOT be re-included.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets are supplied at runtime through environment variables
# (ConnectionStrings__Default, Jwt__Key, ...) — never baked in.
#
# Every appsettings file is excluded first, then each host's own appsettings.json is
# re-included, and nothing else. They are tracked in git
# precisely because they document the configuration schema and hold no secret
# (secret-shaped keys are empty strings), and shipping them keeps the image's
# Logging / Identity / Jwt / Files defaults intact. They are not optional: they are the only place
# Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Database.Command is pinned to Warning, and without them
# the image logs every SQL statement — parameters included — at Information.
# Everything else stays out — in particular
# appsettings.Development.json, which legitimately holds a real local password,
# and any appsettings.Production.json a developer drops in locally.
**/appsettings*.json
!Src/Presentation/AppTemplate.Api/appsettings.json
#if (presentationBlazorServer || presentationMcp)
!Src/Presentation/AppTemplate.PresentationApp/appsettings.json
#endif
#if (jobsWorker)
!Src/Presentation/AppTemplate.Worker/appsettings.json
#endif

**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/secrets.json
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
ex.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and CI — never needed to compile, and .git carries credentials
# in .git/config plus the entire history of every file ever committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
.github/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. Copying host bin/obj into the image poisons the container build
# with artifacts from a different SDK/RID and defeats layer caching.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin
**/obj
**/out
**/TestResults
**/coverage*
**/*.user
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.suo
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests. The runtime image publishes AppTemplate.Api; test
# projects (and the Testcontainers fixtures they carry) are built in CI, not in
# these images.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tests/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs and repository furniture.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md
**/*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE / tooling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Container and orchestration definitions. Excluding these means editing
# docker-compose.yml does not invalidate the build cache.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
**/azds.yaml
**/charts

#if (sqlite)
# The local SQLite database: the container keeps its own on the db-data volume.
**/App_Data/

#endif
#if (anyWeb)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The web workspace: each web app builds from Src/Web with its own image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Src/Web/
#if (webBlazorWasm)
# The WebAssembly app builds from here, beside the solution's props and the .NET client.
!Src/Web/apps/FrameworkSite/
Src/Web/apps/FrameworkSite/bin/
Src/Web/apps/FrameworkSite/obj/
#endif
#endif
